  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> be a point on an argand plane equidistant from the roots of the equation <math><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><msup><mrow><mi>z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math> then the value of&nbsp;<math><mi>h</mi></math> is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "lPQUq",
      "text": "<math><mn>0</mn></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "IWqb8",
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "0vPcG",
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "i65xD",
      "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>z</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>z</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> or <math><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math> or <math><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></math> or <math><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>i</mi></math><br />Hence, the roots are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/760e8876-50da-4389-9213-4fff21130e41.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:2.32014in;height:1.39375in\" /></p><p>i.e. the roots are equidistant from the centre of the circle as shown in the figure.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is the centre of the circle.</p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p>",
